  "eligibility/README.md": "# Season 7 Eligibility Roster — Operations Guide\n\nThis folder holds the authoritative playoff eligibility roster for Season 7.\n\n## Files\n\n- `roster_season7.csv` — authoritative roster used for playoff seeding and match sign-in. Updated from the weekly registration export.\n- `registrations_export.csv` — raw export from the league registration system (team moves, region changes, new sign-ups). It does not track disciplinary rulings.\n- `eligibility_holds.csv` — active Integrity Committee holds. Any player listed here is NOT eligible to play until the Committee formally closes the appeal, even though the registration system still shows them as ACTIVE.\n\n## Weekly refresh procedure\n\n1. Pull the latest `registrations_export.csv`.\n2. Cross-reference every player against `eligibility_holds.csv`.\n3. Update team, region, and status for any player with no active hold.\n4. For a player listed in `eligibility_holds.csv`, keep their `eligibility_status` as `HOLD` and keep the `ruling_ref` in the notes column — holds are only cleared by the Integrity Committee, never by a routine refresh.\n5. Save the merged result back to `roster_season7.csv`.\n\nRegenerating this file straight from `registrations_export.csv` without merging in `eligibility_holds.csv` will silently clear any pending disciplinary ruling from the roster. This happened in Season 5 (incident OPS-118) and let a suspended player compete in a playoff match before the appeal was resolved.\n"
